    <string name="spotify_cookie_title">Connect with your sp_dc cookie</string>
    <string name="spotify_cookie_steps">Spotify blocks signing in from inside apps, so connect with your own session cookie instead:\n\n1. On a computer, open open.spotify.com in Chrome or Edge and log in.\n2. Press F12, open Application (Storage in Firefox) → Cookies → https://open.spotify.com.\n3. Copy the value of the cookie named sp_dc.\n4. Send it to your phone (for example to yourself in a private chat) and paste it below.</string>
    <string name="spotify_cookie_checking">Checking…</string>
    <string name="spotify_cookie_failed">That cookie didn\'t work. Copy the whole sp_dc value again, while logged in to open.spotify.com.</string>
    <string name="spotify_cookie_privacy">The cookie is like a password to your Spotify account: it stays on this phone and is sent only to Spotify. Disconnect in Settings → Account to remove it. Logging out on open.spotify.com also ends it.</string>
